these situations, developers often fall back on implementing a deny list. A deny list is used to selectively reject or 
escape potentially dangerous characters before using the input. However, a list of unsafe characters can quickly 
become incomplete or outdated. A better approach is to create a list of characters that are permitted to appear in log 
entries and accept input composed exclusively of characters in the approved set. The most critical character in most 
log forging attacks is the '\n' (newline) character, which should never appear on a log entry allow list. 
